// spec: SRC-002, SRC-005
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
//
// SRC-005 admits 'unicode_letter' -- what Unicode CLASSIFIES as a letter -- so
// this program must be refused with
// '[line N] Error: Unexpected character: 🙂'.
//
// The scanner admits every code point above 127 instead, so it runs and prints
// 1.
//
// ⚠️ Introduced deliberately, in the direction that keeps correct programs
// working.  The scanner used to refuse every non-ASCII byte, so no Unicode
// letter could appear in a program at all; admitting them all over-accepts,
// where refusing them all under-accepted.  Narrowing it needs a table of the
// letter ranges, which nothing in this compiler has.

var 🙂 := 1;
WriteLn (🙂);
